 local (1,1), (1,2) and (1,4) set to 1.\n\nEmits:\n- the motif recovered by voting;\n- the final grid after marking the erased cells.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    boxes = [b for b in panels(g) if (b[2]-b[0]+1, b[3]-b[1]+1) == (5, 5)]\n    tiles = np.array([crop(g, *b) for b in boxes])\n    h, w = tiles.shape[1:]\n    motif = np.zeros((h, w), dtype=int)\n    for y in range(h):\n        for x in range(w):\n            vals, cnts = np.unique(tiles[:, y, x], return_counts=True)\n            motif[y, x] = vals[np.argmax(cnts)]\n    emit(motif.copy(), \"Majority vote over all panels recovers the intact repeating motif.\")\n    out = motif.copy()\n    diff = (tiles != motif[None]).any(axis=0)\n    out[diff] = 1\n    emit(out.copy(), \"Cells erased in the damaged panel are marked with colour 1.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"panels":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"the grid is made of.** Each input is 29×29 and is cut by full lines of colour 3 into a 5×5 array of panels."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each panel is 5×5."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Almost every panel is an identical copy of one small motif on background 8."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Almost every panel is an identical copy of one small motif on background 8."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**What is different.** In every pair, exactly one panel has a few of its motif cells blanked out to the background colour:"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**What the output is.** The output is the clean 5×5 motif, with colour 1 on exactly the cells that were erased in the damaged panel."}],"repair":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"is.** The output is the clean 5×5 motif, with colour 1 on exactly the cells that were erased in the damaged panel."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"The single damaged panel is outvoted everywhere."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Cells erased in the damaged panel are marked with colour 1."}],"boolean":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**What is different.** In every pair, exactly one panel has a few of its motif cells blanked out to the background colour:"}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"051b4a13bc4fc8fedaf66b80f8780f9f8ca76eea20518aeb8029fa8b5a0d1860","task_sha256":"3c37418235611e0e89a175c284c41ef31cec5e9f3fa15f086caa9a61431273a7","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
